@startuml
title statlord System Architecture

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam wrapWidth 240
skinparam maxMessageSize 240

actor "API Client" as ApiClient

node "User Browser" as Browser {
  component "Editor SPA\n(TypeScript/React)" as Editor
  component "Viewer Page" as ViewerClient
  component "Redux Store" as Redux
  Editor -- Redux : State mgmt
}

device "Display Device\n(OLED / e-paper / LCD)" as DisplayDevice
node "Headless Renderer\n(optional)" as Headless

node "Dev Container (development-grade)\n- Python 3.7 base\n- Node.js + npm\n- Django runserver" as DevContainer {
  node "Django Server" as Django {
    component "Static Assets Server" as Static
    component "REST API" as API
    component "Gauges Service" as Gauges
    component "Displays Service" as Displays
    component "Layouts Service" as Layouts
    component "Viewer Renderer\n(Black & White pixels\nat display resolution)" as ViewerSrv
  }
  component "Node.js Build Tooling" as NodeBuild
  artifact "Built Client Assets\n(HTML/CSS/JS)" as Assets
}

database "PostgreSQL" as PG

' Static asset serving
Editor -down-> Static : GET static assets\n(HTML/CSS/JS)
Static -down-> Assets : serves

' Editor interactions with API
Editor --> API : JSON over HTTP(S)\nCRUD Gauges/Displays/Layouts

' Viewer route consumption
ViewerClient --> ViewerSrv : GET /viewer/{displayKey}
DisplayDevice --> ViewerSrv : HTTP(S) GET viewer path\n(render at device resolution)
Headless --> ViewerSrv : Automated rendering\n(headless browser)

' External API clients
ApiClient --> API : POST/GET data\n(gauges, displays, layouts)

' Server-side composition and persistence
API -[hidden]down- Gauges
API -[hidden]down- Displays
API -[hidden]down- Layouts
API --> PG : Persist/query entities
ViewerSrv --> PG : Read display data/layouts

' Build chain within container
NodeBuild ..> Assets : npm install\nnpm run build
Assets ..> Static : deployed as server-served\nstatic content

' Notes describing data contracts and client state
note right of API
Resources (structured JSON):
- Gauge { key, value }
- Display (server) { key, available, resolution_x, resolution_y, current_layout, display_data, rotation }
- Layout { key, data (binary), display_positions (text) }
Persistence:
- PostgreSQL stores Gauge, Display, Layout
Relationships:
- Display.current_layout -> Layout (nullable on deletion)
end note

note right of Redux
Redux-managed state slices:
- controls
- elements
- layouts
- gauges
- displays (client-side Display: { key, available, resolution_x, resolution_y, display_data, rotation })
end note

note right of ViewerSrv
Viewer path:
- Reads Display + Layout
- Produces B/W pixel view at display resolution
end note

note bottom of DevContainer
Supplied containerized deployment:
- Development-grade; not production-ready
- Starts Django with ./manage.py runserver
end note

@enduml
